  "missing": [],
  "notes": "The attr machinery lives in living.c/living.h; the potion map deliberately reproduces the Java 8 HashMap bucket order. The isClientWorld getter is vanilla-misnamed and returns !worldObj.isClient; living_is_client_world copies that. lane/idxentity: stale items (already ported): the sprint boost, jumpMovementFactor, rayTrace, removePotionEffectClient; onItemPickup is the client S0D (a client follow-up). Real gaps fixed: the kill credit (addToPlayerScore to func_94060_bK's killer apart from DamageSource.getEntity()'s onKillEntity; a zombie that dies in lava after the player's punch gives mobKills but no killEntity stat; master's lane/idxblocks landed the same fix, kept on the merge, and ent-kill-s1 pins it too), the arrow decay, the held-item modifier on a pickup (ent-loot-s42), decreaseAirSupply's respiration roll on mobs and the player and the water-breathing gate on the player (ent-water-s1), the pigman being undead for potions (ent-water-s1), renderBrokenItemStack on a sun-broken helmet and no draw for an undamageable one (ent-kill-s1). lane/reloadstate: a living loaded from a chunk starts with potionsNeedUpdate true (the field's initializer), so a reloaded mob with an effect sets its colour on its first update and its particle roll draws the Random (snapshot_entities.c restore_living_nbt; mobs-reload-s1 failed on master at row 170)."
}
